### Siezal Vendor Integration API — manual requests
### VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above each block.
### JetBrains IDEs support this file natively.

@baseUrl = https://apis.siezal.com
@clientId = vendor_IPOS_f3EoSUCc8f
@clientSecret = 7RaktpghRVhK00EjE5zGx9IAhR2LdUSVGubHK2wHKZ1gePAx
@branchId = 1
@categorySlug = soft-drinks

### 1. Login -> captures {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/integrations/vendor/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientId": "{{clientId}}",
  "clientSecret": "{{clientSecret}}"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### 2. List active branches
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/integrations/vendor/branches
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. List imported products (paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/integrations/vendor/products?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Search products by title / SKU / category
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/integrations/vendor/products?page=1&limit=10&q=sprite
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Filter products by branch
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/integrations/vendor/products?page=1&limit=10&branchId={{branchId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Create a product  (WRITES TO THE LIVE CATALOG)
# Rules: (sku, branchId) must be unique; categorySlug must exist;
# stockQuantity:0 forces status -> out_of_stock; gstFee ignored unless isGstEnabled:true.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/integrations/vendor/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "TEST-VENDOR-0001",
  "title": "Vendor API Test Product",
  "categorySlug": "{{categorySlug}}",
  "price": 100,
  "salePrice": 90,
  "stockQuantity": 12,
  "status": "available",
  "branchId": {{branchId}},
  "unit": "piece",
  "isGstEnabled": true,
  "gstFee": 18,
  "shortDescription": "Created via REST Client"
}

### 7. Update a product by SKU  (WRITES — matched by path SKU + body branchId)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/integrations/vendor/products/TEST-VENDOR-0001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "branchId": {{branchId}},
  "price": 150,
  "stockQuantity": 5
}
